relation Expr_ok: p TC |- expression'' : %

1. Block (3 arms)

Arm 1:

  1. Group literalExpression: p TC |- expression'' : %

    1. Case analysis on expression''

      1. Case (let booleanLiteral be %, % has type booleanLiteral)

        1. (Let expressionNoteIR be (`( ((BOOL) as typeIR) (LCTK) `)))

        2. Result in: % % |- % : ((booleanLiteral as expressionIR) '#' expressionNoteIR)

      2. Case (let integerLiteral be %, % has type integerLiteral)

        1. Case analysis on integerLiteral

          1. Case (let (D i) be %, % matches pattern `D %`)

            1. (Let expressionNoteIR be (`( ((INT) as typeIR) (LCTK) `)))

            2. Result in: % % |- % : (((D i) as expressionIR) '#' expressionNoteIR)

          2. Case (let (n S i) be %, % matches pattern `% S %`)

            1. (Let expressionNoteIR be (`( ((INT `< n `>) as typeIR) (LCTK) `)))

            2. Result in: % % |- % : (((n S i) as expressionIR) '#' expressionNoteIR)

          3. Case (let (n W i) be %, % matches pattern `% W %`)

            1. (Let expressionNoteIR be (`( ((BIT `< n `>) as typeIR) (LCTK) `)))

            2. Result in: % % |- % : (((n W i) as expressionIR) '#' expressionNoteIR)

      3. Case (let stringLiteral be %, % has type stringLiteral)

        1. (Let expressionNoteIR be (`( ((STRING) as typeIR) (LCTK) `)))

        2. Result in: % % |- % : ((stringLiteral as expressionIR) '#' expressionNoteIR)

