def $result_concat(typeIR, typeIR')

1. Block (2 arms)

Arm 1:

  1. Case analysis on typeIR

    1. Case (let stringTypeIR be %, % has type stringTypeIR)

      1. (Let stringTypeIR' be typeIR', typeIR' has type stringTypeIR)

        1. Return ((STRING) as typeIR)

    2. Case (let (INT `< w_a `>) be %, % has type fixedIntTypeIR)

      1. Case analysis on typeIR'

        1. Case (let (INT `< w_b `>) be %, % has type fixedIntTypeIR)

          1. Return ((INT `< (w_a + w_b) `>) as typeIR)

        2. Case (let (BIT `< w_b `>) be %, % has type fixedBitTypeIR)

          1. Return ((INT `< (w_a + w_b) `>) as typeIR)

      1. Else Dangling#8951

    3. Case (let (BIT `< w_a `>) be %, % has type fixedBitTypeIR)

      1. Case analysis on typeIR'

        1. Case (let (INT `< w_b `>) be %, % has type fixedIntTypeIR)

          1. Return ((BIT `< (w_a + w_b) `>) as typeIR)

        2. Case (let (BIT `< w_b `>) be %, % has type fixedBitTypeIR)

          1. Return ((BIT `< (w_a + w_b) `>) as typeIR)

      1. Else Dangling#8957

    4. Case (let (TYPEDEF _typeId typeIR_l) be %, % has type typedefTypeIR)

      1. Return $result_concat(typeIR_l, typeIR')

  1. Else Dangling#8945

Arm 2:

  1. (Let (TYPEDEF _typeId typeIR_r) be typeIR', typeIR' has type typedefTypeIR)

    1. If (~(typeIR has type typedefTypeIR)), then

      1. Return $result_concat(typeIR, typeIR_r)

    1. Else Dangling#8966

